<title>POLAND: ComputerLand up on Siemens deal.</title>
<headline>ComputerLand up on Siemens deal.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish software firm ComputerLand SA jumped 6.7 percent to 96 zlotys in moderate trade on Wednesday, buoyed by Tuesday's news it would market and sell Siemens Nixdorf products, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The stock had been rising of late but the Siemens news must have had an extra psychological effect,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Siemens Nixdorf is the computers unit of German electronics and engineering giant Siemens AG.</p>
<p>One trader said the stock could slow its growth in the short term as its 26.7 price-earnings ratio based on estimated 1997 earnings looked a little high, but that both stock and firm had good medium and long-term prospects.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
